# Exploring IoT Devices

In Lesson 10, your students start an activity by comparing devices that work on their own with devices that connect to the Internet. Try the comparison yourself before you teach it.

<div style="background-color:#F7F7FB; border-left:4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius:8px; padding:12px 16px; margin:20px 0;">
<p>📖 <strong>Internet of Things (IoT)</strong>: a network of smart devices that connect and share data over the Internet</p>
</div>

## Compare a Device Pair

Choose one standalone device and one IoT device below. Answer these questions for each device you choose:

<p>• What types of data does this device collect, and how might it be used?</p>
<p>• How might it transmit data, if at all?</p>
<p>• What privacy risks might it introduce?</p>
<p>• With Internet connectivity, how might its functionality change?</p>

<div style="display:flex; gap:20px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin:20px 0;">
<div style="flex:1; min-width:260px; background-color:#F7F7FB; border:1px solid #E4E2F8; border-radius:10px; padding:16px;">
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; color:#1F1976;">Standalone Device</div>
<p>Runs locally without external data sharing</p>
<div style="display:flex; gap:12px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:12px;">
<div style="flex:1; min-width:120px; background-color:#FFFFFF; border:1px solid #ACA8EA; border-radius:10px; padding:12px; text-align:center;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/444c213457ae28e39ba548f0dc022a30-image-1791910025087.png" alt="A small pedometer that counts steps" style="width:100px; height:auto; border-radius:10px; display:block; margin:0 auto 10px auto;">
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; color:#222222;">Pedometer</div>
</div>
<div style="flex:1; min-width:120px; background-color:#FFFFFF; border:1px solid #ACA8EA; border-radius:10px; padding:12px; text-align:center;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/c19d67b136faf7fd3461cde9f350e26a-image-1791909758846.png" alt="A handheld digital thermometer showing a temperature reading" style="width:100px; height:auto; border-radius:10px; display:block; margin:0 auto 10px auto;">
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; color:#222222;">Digital thermometer</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="flex:1; min-width:260px; background-color:#E4E2F8; border:1px solid #ACA8EA; border-radius:10px; padding:16px;">
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; color:#1F1976;">Internet of Things (IoT) Device</div>
<p>Communicates with the Internet for additional functionality</p>
<div style="display:flex; gap:12px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:12px;">
<div style="flex:1; min-width:120px; background-color:#FFFFFF; border:1px solid #ACA8EA; border-radius:10px; padding:12px; text-align:center;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/17a56695a56f5d2f273a7563724ebde7-image-1791909365860.png" alt="A cylindrical smart speaker with a light ring" style="width:100px; height:auto; border-radius:10px; display:block; margin:0 auto 10px auto;">
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; color:#222222;">Smart speaker</div>
</div>
<div style="flex:1; min-width:120px; background-color:#FFFFFF; border:1px solid #ACA8EA; border-radius:10px; padding:12px; text-align:center;">
<img src="https://images.code.org/cf0b8eb49daa45b4866781ae13b1f453-image-1791909566738.png" alt="A video doorbell camera mounted beside a front door" style="width:100px; height:auto; border-radius:10px; display:block; margin:0 auto 10px auto;">
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; color:#222222;">Video doorbell camera</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="background-color:#E4E2F8; color:#222222; border-radius:10px; padding:14px 16px; margin:20px 0;">
<p><strong>💡 Teacher tip:</strong> The goal of this comparison is for students to see that they already use IoT devices in everyday life, such as a smartwatch that sends step counts to a phone app or a thermostat that adjusts to the weather outside. Invite students to name devices from their own lives before you share these examples.</p>
</div>



